  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Bridges: Women Peacebuilders reclaim Peace, Redefine Security - Outcome 4 - preventing and combatting violent extremism and terrorism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project&#x2019;s expected effect(s) on society is to prevent and solve violent conflicts and building lasting peace. The project aims to ensure that peace and reconciliation processes facilitate participation by women-led CSOs and WPBs in all phases and that, with their support, the implementation of peace agreements safeguards the rights of both women and men (Impact).

Support to new outcome 4: Women-les CSOs and WPBs involved are strenghtened and have greater impact in preventing and combatting violent extremism and terrorism.

Countries include: Albania, Lebanon, Iraq and Indonesia.</narrative>
  </description>
